	(text "R4/R23 DNP is an assembly hold, NOT full isolation; I/O and LEDA can still be connected.\nDo not connect B until VCI, VDD, LED Vf max and total IF are confirmed.\nOne shunt only. Missing shunt: ~10.39 V OVP fallback, not a shutdown interlock.\nJP1 selects protection threshold; U1 still regulates CURRENT. OVP transients need tests.\nJ3 is HOST CN2 ONLY: .1=3V3 / .6=GND; panel touch tail .1=GND / .6=3V3.\nNever plug a panel tail into J3. Use J2.32-35 only after internal routing is confirmed.\nReview GT911 startup INT behavior, both supply budgets and exact TI U2 limits."
		(at 16.0 247.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
